        "Session contains 'I went to a LGBTQ support group yesterday' → memory stores only greeting fragment, not the declarative statement",
        "Session contains 'I'm doing kickboxing' → memory stores only 'Just got back from a...', ignoring subsequent informative clauses",
        "Ground truth 'Psychology, counseling certification' has no basis in stored memories — no education-related content was ingested"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "recommendations": [
    {
      "skill_change": "Implement fact-aware memory segmentation",
      "concrete_action": "Replace naive sliding-window or prefix-based memory chunking with NLP-driven segmentation: split on sentence boundaries, prioritize declarative utterances (SVO clauses), and explicitly extract temporal expressions, activities, and domains using dependency parsing and NER. Store full sentences like 'Caroline: I went to a LGBTQ support group yesterday.' instead of truncated greetings."
    },
    {
      "skill_change": "Introduce retrieval-time query expansion with temporal and semantic anchors",
      "concrete_action": "Augment user questions during retrieval with synonyms and temporal patterns (e.g., 'When did X happen?' → expand to ['date', 'on [DATE]', 'yesterday', 'last week', 'May 2023', '21 December 2022']); use hybrid retrieval (keyword + embedding) to boost recall of time-anchored and activity-bearing fragments."
    },
    {
      "skill_change": "Add memory validation and coverage auditing",
      "concrete_action": "At ingestion time, run a lightweight QA oracle over each session to identify all answerable factoid questions (e.g., 'What did X do?', 'When did Y happen?') and verify their presence in stored memories; flag and re-ingest sessions where >20% of ground-truth facts are missing from memory."
    }
  ]
